        <hr class="my-4">
        <h5 class="fw-bold mb-1"><i class="fas fa-list-ol me-2"></i><span class="ds-i18n">How to Use — Step-by-Step Instructions</span></h5>
        <p class="text-muted small mb-3 ds-i18n">Follow these steps in order for the best calibration results.</p>

        <div class="card mb-3">
          <div class="card-body">
            <h6 class="card-title fw-bold ds-i18n">Step 1 — Calibrate Stick Center</h6>
            <p class="card-text mb-0 ds-i18n">Set your controller flat on a surface and <strong>do not touch the thumbsticks.</strong> Let them rest completely on their own. Then press <em>Calibrate Stick Center.</em> This locks in the true neutral resting position of both sticks and is the most effective correction for stick drift.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="card mb-3">
          <div class="card-body">
            <h6 class="card-title fw-bold ds-i18n">Step 2 — Calibrate Stick Range</h6>
            <p class="card-text mb-0 ds-i18n">Press <em>Calibrate Stick Range,</em> then slowly rotate <strong>both thumbsticks in smooth, wide circles,</strong> covering the full outer edge of their range. Complete a minimum of <strong>2 full rotations on each stick in both clockwise and counter-clockwise directions.</strong> Keep going until the <em>Done</em> button appears. This teaches the device the exact travel limits of your sticks for accurate input mapping.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="card mb-3">
          <div class="card-body">
            <h6 class="card-title fw-bold ds-i18n">Step 3 — Fine-Tune Stick Center <span class="text-muted fw-normal">(Optional)</span></h6>
            <p class="card-text mb-0 ds-i18n">Press <em>Finetune Stick Calibration</em> and use the <strong>D-Pad</strong> to micro-adjust the center point of each stick. Use this step only if you notice a slight offset after completing Steps 1 and 2.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="card mb-4">
          <div class="card-body">
            <h6 class="card-title fw-bold ds-i18n">Step 4 — Save Your Calibration</h6>
            <p class="card-text mb-0 ds-i18n">Once you are satisfied with the results, press <em>Save Changes Permanently.</em> Your calibration is written directly to the controller and will be retained even after it is powered off or disconnected.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="p-3 rounded text-center" style="background-color: #000; color: #fff;">
